    <string name="app_shortcuts_section_discovered">What the app offers</string>
    <string name="app_shortcuts_discovered_note">Shortcuts this app shows when you long-press its icon, and its settings screen, read from the app on this phone. Ctrl+Alt+1 to 4 open the first four (on a keyboard without a number row, hold Ctrl+Alt and press the keys that type 1 to 4), Ctrl+, opens its settings, and one named like New or Search fills Ctrl+N or Ctrl+F when nothing else does.</string>
    <string name="app_shortcuts_discovered_none">This app offers no shortcuts or settings screen to other apps.</string>
    <string name="app_shortcuts_keys_note">Shown as you press them on your keyboard. Where it has no number or \"/\" key, hold Ctrl and Alt with the letter that types it (shown in brackets). Shortcuts your keyboard can\'t make, like arrows without arrow keys, aren\'t listed.</string>
